supermon-ng (4.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix services failing after the 4.4.0 upgrade on systems migrated from the
    old tarball installer. Its unit files in /etc/systemd/system override the
    packaged units and still pointed into /var/www/html/supermon-ng, so the
    backend, websocket, database-update and node-status services failed with
    CHDIR/STDOUT errors once that directory was removed. postinst now moves
    those units (and their paired timers) to
    /var/backups/supermon-ng-legacy-units-*, repoints their enable links at
    the packaged units and reloads systemd before restarting services.
    Systems already broken on 4.4.0 are repaired by this upgrade.
  * Fix the menu bar going empty after login when a user's mapped INI in
    authini.inc does not exist: fall back to allmon.ini, and keep the mapping
    consistent when it is looked up more than once in a request.

 -- Jory A. Pratt <geekypenguin@gmail.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 15:43:00 +0000

supermon-ng (4.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Install to /usr/share/supermon-ng so the site is served outside
    /var/www/html, where the ASL3 appliance's fallback rewrite ignored our
    Apache config. Configs live in /etc/supermon-ng (conffiles), data in
    /var/lib/supermon-ng and logs in /var/log/supermon-ng, linked into the
    app tree.
  * Upgrades from earlier releases migrate .env, user_files, the
    announcement library, database, astdb.txt and logs, rewrite old paths
    in .env, the supermon-ng Apache site and announcement crontab entries,
    archive leftovers to /var/backups/supermon-ng-legacy-*.tar.gz and remove
    /var/www/html/supermon-ng. The old directory is kept if migration fails
    or an enabled Apache config still references it.
  * Helper scripts moved from user_files/sbin to /usr/share/supermon-ng/sbin;
    node_info.ini moved to user_files.
  * Depend on asl3-asterisk, php-apcu, sox, libsox-fmt-mp3 and asl3-tts
    instead of recommending them.
  * Harden the root-run announcement helpers: only the announcement library
    and Asterisk sounds directories are accepted, library files are handled
    as www-data, TTS runs only asl-tts, voice downloads go only to
    /var/lib/piper-tts, playback survives sudo's pty closing, and the
    schedule lock moved to /run/lock without hiding script errors.
  * Node status: sanitize WX text, disable config interpolation, always
    remove the alert temp file, and log to /var/log/supermon-ng.
  * din, ssinfo and dvswitch-bridge-restart.sh fixes: df -t and -P output,
    DHCP detection, CPU speed, global.inc lookup, single restart per unit.
  * din: fix the disk table on systems using mawk (Raspberry Pi OS), where
    an invalid printf format dropped the mount point and row breaks.
  * ssinfo: read $LOCATION, $TITLE2 and $TITLE3 from global.inc with HTML
    removed instead of matching comment lines, and skip the login history
    quietly when last is not installed (trixie).

 -- Jory A. Pratt <geekypenguin@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:18:00 +0000

supermon-ng (4.3.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix announcement uploads always failing with "No file uploaded." The
    shared API client's JSON Content-Type made axios serialize the upload
    FormData to JSON, dropping the file. FormData requests now go out as
    multipart/form-data with the browser-set boundary.
  * Raise backend upload limits: supermon-ng-backend now starts php -S with
    upload_max_filesize=32M and post_max_size=33M. The php-cli defaults (2M)
    were below the 10 MB announcement max_bytes.
  * Docs: note the backend upload limit alongside max_bytes in
    docs/ANNOUNCEMENTS.md.

 -- Jory A. Pratt <geekypenguin@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:26:00 +0000

supermon-ng (4.3.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Subdirectory installs (/supermon-ng) no longer install a supermon-ng site
    or disable 000-default / default-ssl. On ASL3 images those default sites
    carry the appliance's own settings; they are now left enabled and
    untouched, and the app is served from the global
    conf-available/supermon-ng.conf under whichever site answers.
  * The global conf also copies /supermon-ng requests to
    /var/log/apache2/supermon-ng_access.log (GlobalLog). Errors stay in the
    serving site's error.log, which the dashboard log viewer reads.
  * If no enabled site listens on port 80 or 443, 000-default / default-ssl
    (snakeoil) are enabled; use certbot --apache for a real certificate.
  * Upgrades disable a supermon-ng site from an earlier release and move it
    to supermon-ng.conf.bak only when it exactly matches a generated
    subdirectory site (any past release) or a generated root-mode site with
    no ServerName or Let's Encrypt certificate. Customized sites, and
    generated root-mode sites with a ServerName or Let's Encrypt certificate,
    are kept (with a warning for the latter).
  * Generated root-mode sites are recognized from the ServerName and
    certificate recorded in the site, not the current .env.
  * Root-mode redirect conflicts are detected by testing each RedirectMatch
    against the actual APP_BASE_PATH (e.g. /supermon-ng2).
  * "Disable default sites" now applies only to APP_BASE_PATH=/; the
    regenerate prompt retires the site in subdirectory mode. setenvif is
    enabled for the access log. Purge also removes supermon-ng.conf.bak.
  * Root mode (APP_BASE_PATH=/) behavior is unchanged.

 -- Jory A. Pratt <geekypenguin@gmail.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:20:00 +0000

supermon-ng (4.3.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix /supermon-ng returning 404 on ASL3 appliance 3.x hosts. asl3-appliance
    3.0.0 installs 000-asl3-appliance sites without a ServerName, which become
    Apache's default vhost and shadow the supermon-ng site.
  * Subdirectory mode now installs its Alias/ProxyPass routes as a global
    conf (/etc/apache2/conf-available/supermon-ng.conf, a2enconf), applied
    under every vhost; the supermon-ng site becomes a host-only vhost. The
    conf is regenerated from .env on every configure. Root mode
    (APP_BASE_PATH=/) keeps its dedicated vhost and removes the conf.
  * The API proxy sets X-Forwarded-Proto from the request scheme, so Secure
    cookies and wss:// work behind the appliance's TLS vhost.
  * Scope config/apache-performance.conf to the app's public directory so its
    headers and caching do not leak onto other sites on the host.
  * Place the /supermon-ng/user_files Alias before /supermon-ng so it matches
    (served behind user_files/.htaccess Basic Auth, as in root mode); removes
    the AH00671 configtest warning.
  * configure-apache: when switching to APP_BASE_PATH=/, replace the host-only
    subdirectory site (backup kept) instead of leaving no routes. When
    switching to /supermon-ng, replace the generated root-mode site, or stop
    with instructions if a customized one would redirect the path away.
  * configure-apache: warn when root mode has no ServerName on hosts with the
    ASL3 appliance default sites.
  * prerm/postrm: disable the conf on remove and delete it on purge.
  * WebSocket: reconnect AMI after Asterisk restarts. Failed XStat/SawStat
    actions now drop the dead socket so the next poll reconnects (closes #28);
    the first failure skips the 30-second reconnect backoff.
  * Docs: document the global Apache conf in README, docs/DEBIAN.md, and the
    debconf template.

 -- Jory A. Pratt <geekypenguin@gmail.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:25:00 +0000

